            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Não foi possível mudar o ícone"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Count new leaves": {
      "comment": "Care guide step title; short",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Conte as folhas novas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Couple": {
      "comment": "Household type; max 14 chars",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Casal"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cozy season. One last meal, then let them rest.": {
      "comment": "Autumn tip",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Estação aconchegante. Uma última adubada e depois deixe elas descansarem."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Curious": {
      "comment": "Plant personality name",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Curiosa"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Curling": {
      "comment": "Care guide step title; short",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Enrolando"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Curling leaves usually mean I'm thirsty, the air is too dry, or I'm getting too much sun. %@": {
      "comment": "Plant chat: curling leaves. %@ = species light rule sentence.",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Folhas enrolando geralmente significam sede, ar seco demais ou sol demais. %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut 1 cm below the node. The node is where roots will grow.": {
      "comment": "Care guide step instruction; warm, practical",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte 1 cm abaixo do nó. É do nó que saem as raízes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut a green spike just above a node to encourage a side branch, or cut a brown one at the base.": {
      "comment": "Care guide step instruction; warm, practical",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte uma haste verde logo acima de um nó para estimular um galho lateral, ou corte uma haste seca rente à base."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut about 1 cm above a node at a slight angle. For a dead leaf, cut its stalk at the base.": {
      "comment": "Care guide step instruction; warm, practical",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte cerca de 1 cm acima de um nó, levemente inclinado. Para uma folha seca, corte o cabinho na base."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut above it": {
      "comment": "Care guide step title; short",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte acima dele"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut and pot": {
      "comment": "Care guide step title; short",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte e plante"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut below the moss ball and plant it whole. The old stem will sprout again.": {
      "comment": "Care guide step instruction; warm, practical",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte abaixo da bola de musgo e plante tudo junto. O caule antigo vai brotar de novo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut below the node": {
      "comment": "Care guide step title; short",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte abaixo do nó"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut if needed": {
      "comment": "Care guide step title; short",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte se precisar"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cut just below a node (the bump where a leaf meets the stem), with 1–2 leaves. Keep it warm, in bright indirect light. Change the water weekly.": {
      "comment": "Propagation instructions",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Corte logo abaixo de um nó (o calombinho onde a folha encontra o caule), com 1–2 folhas. Deixe em lugar quentinho, com luz indireta forte. Troque a água toda semana."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cutting": {
      "comment": "Fact value: grown from a cutting; max 12 chars\nPropagation row title when parent plant is gone",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Muda"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cutting taken": {
      "comment": "Propagation stage; short",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Muda cortada"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cuttings": {
      "comment": "Me shortcut title: propagation cuttings",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mudas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dab each cluster with cotton and rubbing alcohol": {
      "comment": "Pest treatment step; imperative, short; max 70 chars",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Passe algodão com álcool em cada bolinho"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dab mealybugs with alcohol on a cotton bud. Spray soap or neem on the rest, following the label.": {
      "comment": "Care guide step instruction; warm, practical",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Passe álcool nas cochonilhas com um cotonete. Borrife sabão ou neem no resto, seguindo o rótulo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Daisy, Sunny, Goldie": {
      "comment": "Comma-separated pet-name ideas for a plant; give local, playful names a native would pick, same count",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Margô, Solzinho, Dourada"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Damp: foggy windows, mould spots": {
      "comment": "Home air humidity option in Settings.",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Úmido: janela embaçada, mofo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dampen a handful and squeeze. It should hold together, then crumble when poked. If water drips, add more grit or bark.": {
      "comment": "Care guide step instruction; warm, practical",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Umedeça um punhado e aperte. Ele deve ficar firme e se desfazer quando você cutucar. Se pingar água, coloque mais areia ou casca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dates": {
      "comment": "Travel plan section title",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Datas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Day": {
      "comment": "Menu",
      "localizations": {
        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dia"
          }
        }
      }
